  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting children and their families in cholera and cyclone FREDDY affected areas with WASH and Health lifesaving interventions</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide WASH and Health assistance to people affected by floods and cholera in Inhambane, Sofala, Manica, Tete, Zambezia and Niassa provinces. This UNICEF project provides WASH and Health assistance to prevent widespread of water related diseases. The project provides humanitarian assistance to 116,951 people, including 35,085 women, 29,238 men, 52,628 children, and including 7,020 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
